  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - That the London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 25 February 2005 the proposed conversion of existing roof area to provide an additional bedroom to existing first floor flat was NOT lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\t\r\nAs a flat No. 78 Redesdale Gardens does not have any permitted development rights, so that the proposal cannot be assessed under Part 1 of Schedule 2 of The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995, which relates to 'Development within the Curtilage of a Dwellinghouse'.  In that the proposal would constitute development, planning permission is required.\r\n"
